  <title>Purchase order</title>

  <p>Open a purchase order with <guiseq><gui>Vendor</gui><gui>New purchase
  order</gui></guiseq>, the <gui>New Purchase Order</gui> button of the main
  window, or <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>P</key></keyseq>. A vendor has one
  open purchase order at a time: choosing the vendor opens it, or starts one
  with the first line. Everything is saved as you go, so the order can be
  built up over days and posted when it is ready to send.</p>

  <section id="lines">
  <title>Adding products</title>
  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the vendor.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>New</gui>, or press <key>F2</key>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Type the quantity and press <key>Tab</key>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the product from the list or by typing part of its name.
    Its vendor order number, <gui>Stock</gui> and cost are filled
    in.</p></item>
  </steps>
  <p>If you choose a product already on the order, you are asked whether to
  <gui>Update qty</gui> of the existing line, <gui>Add again</gui> as a second
  line, or <gui>Cancel</gui>.</p>
  <p>You can also scan a product's barcode into <gui>Scan barcode</gui>. Each
  scan adds one of the product, on its existing line if the order already has
  one. Barcodes that match no product are collected in the <gui>Barcode
  error!</gui> window.</p>
  <list>
    <item><p><keyseq><key>Shift</key><key>Enter</key></keyseq> after a scan
    takes one off that product's line instead.</p></item>
    <item><p><keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Enter</key></keyseq> after a scan
    changes the selected line to that product.</p></item>
  </list>
  <p>Right click a line to <gui>Delete item</gui> (<key>F3</key>),
  <gui>Move up</gui> or <gui>Move down</gui>
  (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Up</key></keyseq>,
  <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Down</key></keyseq>), or open its <gui>Product
  hub</gui> (<keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>H</key></keyseq>).</p>
  </section>

  <section id="order_number">
  <title>Order numbers</title>
  <p>The <gui>Order number</gui> is the vendor's number for the product. Type
  part of one to pick a product by it. If nothing matches, click the icon in
  the box, or press <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>Enter</key></keyseq>, to
  search every order number ever used; double click a result to use that
  product.</p>
  <p>Changing a line's order number asks whether the change is
  <gui>Permanent</gui>, for this and every later order from this vendor, or
  <gui>Temporary</gui>, for this order only. Check <gui>Remember selection for
  the rest of this purchase order</gui> to stop being asked.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="non_stock">
  <title>Products you have never ordered</title>
  <p>Type a product name that is not in the list and press <key>Enter</key>.
  The <gui>Create non stock product</gui> window offers to make it: give it
  the vendor's <gui>Order number</gui>, a <gui>Default expense account</gui>
  and an <gui>Income account</gui>. It warns if the name or order number is
  already in use.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="vendors">
  <title>Several vendors at once</title>
  <p>Check <gui>View all</gui> to see the open purchase orders of every
  vendor in one list, with a <gui>Vendor</gui> column. Choose another vendor
  for a line to move it onto that vendor's open order.</p>
  <p>Check <gui>Hold</gui> on a line to leave it out of this order. When the
  order is posted, the held lines stay behind on a new open order for the same
  vendor.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="post">
  <title>Posting</title>
  <p>Click <gui>Post Purchase Order</gui>. It prints, through the print dialog
  or straight to the printer if <gui>Direct print</gui> is checked in the
  window menu, and is closed. It then waits in <link xref="unprocessed_po"/>
  for the vendor's invoice. <gui>Post and process</gui> in the window menu
  posts it and opens that window at once.</p>
  <p>To change your mind, check <gui>Cancel printing and posting</gui> on the
  <gui>PyGtk Posting</gui> tab of the print dialog, then click
  <gui>Print</gui>. Nothing is printed or posted, and the order stays open.
  Closing the print dialog with <gui>Cancel</gui> instead still posts the
  order, without printing it. <gui>Direct print</gui> skips the dialog, so
  check the order with <gui>View purchase order</gui> first.</p>
  <p>An order already invoiced cannot be posted again from here; correct it
  in <link xref="vendor_payment"/>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="menu">
  <title>The window menu</title>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Cancel</gui></title>
    <p>Closes the window. The order stays open.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Export to CSV</gui></title>
    <p>Saves the lines not on hold to a spreadsheet file, to send to a vendor
    who takes orders that way.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Products</gui></title>
    <p>Opens the <link xref="products">products</link> window.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>View purchase order</gui></title>
    <p>Shows the order as it would print.</p></item>
  </terms>
  <p>Type a new <gui>PO name</gui> and click the icon in the box to rename the
  order. Drag a line from <link xref="invoice_history"/> or another list onto
  the order to add that product.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="others">
  <title>Changes made on another computer</title>
  <p>If someone else changes the order you have open, a bar says <gui>There
  are changes on this PO</gui>; click <gui>Refresh</gui> to see them. A line
  someone else is editing cannot be changed until they finish.</p>
  </section>

</page>
